From 92f3e1346fc5fddd94e6067853cae6da941b4852 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JavaZeroo <2487163254@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:11:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: gate the SIMT kernel type on Ascend950 in
 NPUTritonKernel

NPUTritonKernel.add_npu_inductor_meta writes

    inductor_meta["npu_kernel_type"] = str(NPUKernelType.SIMD_SIMT_MIX)

unconditionally. Every other place that picks a kernel type gates on the
chip -- NPUIndexTritonKernel.__init__ (triton.py:1017), ir.py:1566,
ir.py:1858 and config.py:319 all check is_ascend950 or
inductor_indirect_memory_mode, which is None off Ascend950 -- so this one
line is the only path that asks for a SIMT mode on 910B2.

The consequence is not a slow kernel but a hard failure. Once
"simd_simt_mix" reaches inductor_meta, the autotuner adds SIMT_ONLY
candidates (runtime/triton_heuristics.py:3360,
runtime/fasta_autotune.py:407), compile_mode="simt_only" reaches the
Triton-Ascend backend, and it appends --enable-triton-ir-compile and
--pure-simt (triton/backends/ascend/compiler.py:1076-1077). No released
bishengir-compile implements those: 1.2.0 as shipped by triton-ascend
3.2.2 and by CANN 9.1.0 has zero SIMT options, hidden ones included. The
user sees

  bishengir-compile: Unknown command line argument '--pure-simt'.
  triton.compiler.errors.MLIRCompilationError:
    [ConvertLinalgRToBinary] encounters error

which reads like a stale CANN and sends people to upgrade the toolkit,
where nothing changes.

Reproduced on 910B2 / CANN 9.1.0 / torch 2.15.0.dev20260812 with
torch.compile over a FlexAttention document mask, which reaches
NPUTritonKernel through NPUNoLinearTritonScheduling
(codegen/scheduling.py:56) after memory-access linearization fails. The
autotune candidates were captured at the subprocess boundary and carry
--num-warps=64/32/16/8, confirming the autotuner as the source.

With this change the SIMT flags are gone and the same kernel fails
further down, in the SIMD path, with

  LLVM ERROR: Failed to obtain op buffer shape size which should be static.

That is the honest limit: indirect load + sum has no lowering on 910B2.
This commit does not claim to make such kernels compile. It stops
torch_npu from requesting a compile mode the platform does not have, so
the reported error points at the real constraint.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WNpsCvjYc85YP4XZkwuAzj
---
 torch_npu/_inductor/codegen/triton.py | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/torch_npu/_inductor/codegen/triton.py b/torch_npu/_inductor/codegen/triton.py
index 6fcfe151d..614ea2303 100644
--- a/torch_npu/_inductor/codegen/triton.py
+++ b/torch_npu/_inductor/codegen/triton.py
@@ -928,7 +928,14 @@ class NPUTritonKernel(TritonKernel):
             axis_names += [tree.prefix for tree in reduction_range_trees]
 
         inductor_meta["requires_no_linear_block_remap"] = True
-        inductor_meta["npu_kernel_type"] = str(NPUKernelType.SIMD_SIMT_MIX)
+        # SIMT compile modes exist only on Ascend950; asking for simd_simt_mix
+        # elsewhere makes the autotuner emit simt_only candidates, whose
+        # --pure-simt / --enable-triton-ir-compile flags no released
+        # bishengir-compile accepts. Mirror the chip gate used everywhere else
+        # (see __init__ of NPUIndexTritonKernel, ir.py, config.py).
+        inductor_meta["npu_kernel_type"] = str(
+            NPUKernelType.SIMD_SIMT_MIX if npu_config.is_ascend950 else NPUKernelType.SIMD
+        )
         inductor_meta["split_axis"] = split_axis
         inductor_meta["tiling_axis"] = tiling_axis
         inductor_meta["low_dims"] = [tiling_axis[-1]]
